{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I acquired</b> — Some say: and I bought her, like תכרו מאתם. But this is not correct in meaning nor in grammar. It is from the root of הכר נא. It should properly have been ואכירה, or it is from the binyan kal even though no kal form of the root הכר is found; behold it is on the pattern of אתנה, or the small patach in place of the big patach, like ואעדך עדי, which is from עדה; פן אכלך בדרך, from כלה. And this word comes in the manner of וידבקו and many like it." "<b>And the meaning of fifteen silver</b> — in its plain sense, for her bride-price." "<b>And barley and spelt</b> — for food. And in my opinion, it is a parable for Judah, and these fifteen are the kings of Judah, whose beginning is Rehoboam the king. And do not count the reign of the sons of Josiah as separate, but as one reign, for they were brothers." "<b>And barley and spelt</b> — these are the high priests who were in the kingdom of Judah in Jerusalem."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:02.148807109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}